    "why": "Source disagreement widens each player's distribution again: sigma^2 is v2.3's fitted line squared plus (alpha * spread)^2, with the spread pulled toward the position's typical spread as if prior_sources more sources had reported it. The 2025 fit found disagreement unpredictive, but it saw at most five sources a week where 2026 has eight, so that finding does not carry; alpha is set by hand at 4 (about 15% wider for a typical starter, 40% for the most disputed) until a fit on 2026 weeks replaces it. The typical spreads are the week-4 medians among starters with five or more sources. The horizon block discounts a roster's edge in later weeks: the playoffs step shrinks each future starter's mu toward the league mean at his position by (1 - 0.05)^weeks_ahead, because injuries and roster moves accumulate and a week-15 lineup is less knowable in week 4 than in week 12. See docs/architecture/03-modeling-and-odds.md, sections 1 and 6.",
    "check": "calibration_metrics for 2026 as the weeks are graded: player and starter 80% coverage near 0.80 under v3 confirms alpha, coverage well above 0.85 says it is too wide; then fit alpha on the graded 2026 weeks."
  },
